          "code": "GET_COST_ANALYSIS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771583275417",
          "id": "1769407301580",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769407301582_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "#Input\n {{$context.$nodes.CALCULATE_VARIENCE.$output.result}} \n#Role\nYou are a Costing and Program Risk analyst. Examine the provided input, which is an array of components  Each entry may include:\nItem number\nCurrent BOM\nTarget BOM\nVariance\nSavings\nThe last array item will be the sub total, which you need to show in a second multiRecord table\n#Guidelines\nProvide a brief, business-formal summary (1-2 sentences, under 50 words) highlighting key insights, such as supply risks, unusual cost data, or patterns in sourcing status. Place this summary immediately before the \"Costing Saving Analysis\" table.\nFor each component, display only these columns: Item number, Current BOM, Target BOM, Variance, Savings.\nIf any data is missing, use \"0\".\nShow results as a formatted multiRecord display.\nFor Variance - highlight with green if it's greater than 30 and orange if it's greater than 0 and red if it's less than 0\nFor Savings - match the color with Variance\nAfter the items, for the last array item (Total) display in a new multiRecord table with headers (Total, Current BOM, Target BOM, Variance, Savings)\n#Output format\nFirst  your summary, then a formatted multiRecord showing the specified columns for each component. and then a formatted multiRecord showing the specified columns for Total\nNote - Incase of no records do not show any widgets. Just inform user that data is not present yet"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Analyze Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771583439100"
          },
          "code": "ANALYZE_INTENT",
          "id": "1771583325654",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771583325657_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You analyze a single user message and decide if it is an explicit directive to set the Application Context (\"App Context\") for an agentic application, as opposed to a regular query.\n\nTask:\n- Inspect the user`s message text.\n- Determine if the user is explicitly instructing to switch focus (e.g., \"switch focus to item SP-1003371, Org V1\").\n- The directive must reference \"Focus\" (case-insensitive; \"SwitchFocus\" without a space also counts) and include a setting-type verb (e.g., set, update, change, configure, apply, use, switch, select, load) targeting that context.\n- Treat as App Context setting even if combined with other content (e.g., extra narration) as long as a valid directive to set App Context is present.\n- Do NOT treat as App Context setting if:\n   - The message merely mentions context without a setting-type verb (e.g., \"app context item SP-1003371\" with no directive).\n- Be case-insensitive and tolerant of punctuation and spacing variations.\n- Identifiers like \"item SP-1003371\" and \"Org V1\" are typical, but their exact values or presence are not required as long as the directive to switch focus is explicit.\n\nOutput:\nOutput only a single JSON object in the exact schema specified below. Do not output any other text, explanations, markdown, or code fences.\n\nReturn exactly this JSON object shape:\n{\n\"UpdateAppContext\": boolean,\n\"ItemNumber\": string,\n\"OrganizationCode\": string\n}\n\nRules:\n\n- UpdateAppContext: true if user wants to switch focus else false,\n- ItemNumber: The item number extracted from user's message. Pass it empty if UpdateAppContext is false or user has not provided\n- OrganizationCode: The organization code from user's message. Pass it empty if UpdateAppContext is false or user has not provided\n\nInput to analyze:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
